      "content": "crest, a measure of linen cloth (OED s.v. crest n.3) | a measure of Britanny cloth (5 ells) (TNA: PRO, E159/177 Recorda Michaelmas m 5) | linen cloth from Britanny, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.^3) | linen cloth from Britanny, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.3) | a crest is a measure of Britanny cloth (5 ells) (TNA: PRO, E159/177 Recorda Michaelmas m 5), so crest cloth is presumably cloth manufactured in Britanny and therefore measured in crests. However, the account states that one piece measuring 100 ulne was imported | a crest is a measure of Britanny cloth (5 ells) (TNA: PRO, E159/177 Recorda Michaelmas m 5), so crest cloth is presumably cloth manufactured in Britanny and therefore measured in crests | linen cloth from Britanny, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.3) | linen cloth from Brittany, so called because measured in crests (= 5 ells) (OED s.v. crest n.3)"
